  "result": "- **Confirmed: schedule.** `config/prod.yaml:2` sets `session_gc_schedule` to `*/10 * * * *`. `session-gc` runs every 10 minutes.\n- **Confirmed: deletion rule.** `auth/session_gc.py:3` sets `IDLE_LIMIT` to 30 minutes. `collect` deletes each session whose `last_seen_at` is older than that.\n- **Corrected: timezone mismatch.** `auth/session_gc.py:7` builds `cutoff` with `datetime.now(timezone.utc)`. `auth/schema.sql:4` types `last_seen_at` as `timestamptz`. Both sides are absolute instants, so no local time is compared and active sessions do not look older than they are.\n- **Corrected: root cause.** The sessions look idle because `last_seen_at` never moves. `edge-proxy/session.py:8` calls `auth_client.touch` only when `touch_on_request` is true, and `config/prod.yaml:1` sets it to false.\n\nThis case is not a clock bug in `session-gc`. `session-gc` works as written, and it receives stale data from `edge-proxy`.\n\n**Question.** Aelita still recommends turning on `touch_on_request` in production. Do we do that, or move the touch into `auth-service`?",
